61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Plan B is out of the question. The late-turn pool is already at a breaking point. I cannot support it.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"Plan D is basically the ferry pilot from eight years ago. It worked then, and it's the most logical step forward.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Plan C is too risky. It involves the pre-war shells. We'll hit voids and the project will stall for months.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,Plan A... it's construction. We could use the ring-fenced construction balance for that. It wouldn't hurt the operating budget.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Sakura,,Plan A is the best! It fixes the mid-city delays and helps people get across the city faster!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"Plan A is manageable. It relies more on the maintenance contract, which I found has some spare capacity.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"Plan A is fine, but Plan D is a proven win. Why gamble on new lanes when we know the fare system works?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, Plan D requires the ferry and rail offices to agree on data. My research shows they still can't agree on anything.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think Plan A is the safest. It uses the money we already have set aside for construction.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Sakura,,Plan A is like a shortcut! It takes away the waiting and the slow parts. It's the most helpful for everyone!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I agree with Toshio. The administrative friction for Plan D would be a nightmare. Plan A is the most rational choice.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"Fine. If the operators are still fighting, then Plan D is a dead end. I'll go with Plan A.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Toshio,,Plan A avoids the pre-war shells and uses delegated roadway consents. It is the only predictable option here.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'm glad... I'm glad we can agree. Plan A doesn't create a future budget war.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Sakura,,Yay! We're all picking Plan A! It's like a little mystery we solved together!,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
